/div>
<h2>Five-agent cost example</h2><p>Using the annual-billing rates checked October 29, 2026, five Growth agents equal US$95 per month equivalent, billed annually (US$1,140 per year before tax and add-ons). Five Pro agents equal US$275 per month equivalent (US$3,300 per year), and five Enterprise agents equal US$445 per month equivalent (US$5,340 per year). These are simple seat calculations from the <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">official rates</a>, not a quote. They exclude AI sessions beyond the included allowance, Copilot, connector tasks, MCP actions, day passes, taxes and any other contracted services.</p>
<h2>Which plan should you choose?</h2><p>Growth is the starting point if ticketing, shared inbox, portal, knowledge base and standard reporting cover your process. Move to Pro only when multilingual support, custom dashboards, intelligent routing, multiple SLA policies or external collaborators solve a real need. Enterprise is easier to justify when you require its audit, sandbox, skill-based routing or domain/IP controls. Do not choose a tier only because it is labelled most popular.</p><p>Confirm that you are pricing Freshdesk, not Freshdesk Omni. Freshworks describes Freshdesk as email-first and Freshdesk Omni as its multichannel option. If you need chat and social channels, request the correct product and quote before comparing vendors.</p>
<h2>Budget checklist</h2><ol><li>Count paid agents and decide whether annual commitment is acceptable.</li><li>Confirm the exact product SKU and billing selector.</li><li>Map each must-have feature to its plan instead of assuming it is included.</li><li>Budget for the one-time 500-session allowance, then model paid packs and their billing-cycle expiry. Confirm the email and chat session definitions that apply to your product.</li><li>Estimate additional AI sessions, Copilot, day passes, connector tasks and MCP actions.</li><li>Include migration, setup, training and any external integration work.</li><li>Recheck the official pricing page and checkout total before approval.</li></ol>
<h2>Compare alternatives before you commit</h2><p>Start with the <a href="/freshdesk/">Freshdesk hub</a> for the product overview. The entry rate is not a fair comparison if another tool includes a free tier or charges by resolved conversation rather than agent seat. Read the <a href="/freshdesk/alternatives/">Freshdesk alternatives guide</a>, <a href="/freshdesk/review/">Freshdesk review</a> and <a href="/freshdesk/how-to-use/">setup guide</a>, then compare <a href="/compare/freshdesk-vs-help-scout/">Freshdesk vs Help Scout</a> before deciding.</p>
<h2>Freshdesk pricing FAQ</h2><h3>What are Freshdesk current prices?</h3><p>The official pricing page checked October 29, 2026 lists Growth at US$19, Pro at US$55 and Enterprise at US$89 per agent/month billed annually.</p><h3>Is there a permanent free plan?</h3><p>The public pricing page lists a 14-day Enterprise trial and does not show a Free plan. Some Freshdesk support docs still reference a Free program, so confirm new-account eligibility with Freshworks.</p><h3>Are Freddy AI Agent sessions unlimited?</h3><p>No. Freshworks says the first 500 Freddy AI Agent sessions are a one-time complimentary allowance for new customers on Growth, Pro or Enterprise. Extra packs cost US$49 per 100 and are valid for the current billing cycle.</p><h3>What add-ons can change the total?</h3><p>Freddy AI Copilot is listed at US$29 per agent/month on Pro and Enterprise; day passes, connector app tasks, MCP actions and extra AI sessions have separate charges.</p>
<h2>Sources and update note</h2><p>All plan and add-on figures above were checked against the <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">official Freshdesk pricing page on October 29, 2026</a>. The public page can change, and this guide is not a sales quote. Confirm the exact SKU, usage allowance and billing period with Freshworks before purchasing.</p>
HTML
