<h2>What is free?</h2><p>The current <a href="https://www.salesloft.com/platform/chat-agents">Salesloft Chat Agents page</a>, checked October 30, 2026, does not list a Drift free plan or trial. Do not treat an older free-trial reference as a current offer without written confirmation from Salesloft.</p>
<h2>Why historic prices are not a safe budget</h2><p>Old Drift price figures still appear on comparison sites and older product pages. They may describe a plan that was available at a different time, not a plan that can be purchased today. This guide does not present those historical figures as current pricing because Salesloft does not publish a current Drift price on the page checked October 30, 2026.</p><p>For an existing customer, the amount on your signed agreement is more relevant than a third-party listing. For a new buyer, the right comparison is the total cost of a current replacement that can cover the workflow you actually need.</p>
<h2>What may cost extra?</h2><p>Salesloft does not publish a current Drift add-on price list on the page checked October 30, 2026. Ask your account team to confirm any charges under your signed agreement. For replacement tools, check seat fees, AI outcomes or conversations, website traffic limits, routing, integrations, onboarding and support before you compare the monthly headline price.</p>
<h2>What will affect the replacement budget?</h2><h3>Seats and team size</h3><p>Count the people who need full access, routing controls, reporting, or administration. Some tools charge per seat, while others include a set number of seats in a workspace price. Compare the same team size across products.</p><h3>AI usage and website traffic</h3><p>Ask whether the product charges by AI outcome, conversation, website visitor, email contact, or credit. A free plan may be enough for a small test but may not cover your normal volume. Include the cost of extra usage in the estimate.</p><h3>Routing, CRM and calendar needs</h3><p>Do not assume a basic live chat plan includes account-based targeting, round-robin routing, CRM write-back, meeting booking or advanced analytics. Identify the features that your current workflow uses and confirm which plan contains them.</p><h3>Migration and parallel running</h3><p>Budget time for exporting records, rebuilding playbooks, mapping fields, configuring the new widget, training sales representatives and testing human handoff. If you need to keep two systems running during a short cutover, confirm any overlap or contract charges with the vendors.</p>
<h2>Where to check current replacement prices</h2><p>The <a href="/drift/alternatives/">Drift alternatives guide</a> compares current options and links to their official pricing pages. The current pages checked October 30, 2026 show different models: Chili Piper publishes starting rates for routing and scheduling; Intercom combines seat and AI outcome charges; Tidio uses conversation and visitor allowances; Crisp uses workspace plans; Qualified and 1mind ask buyers to request a demo or quote; HubSpot offers free live chat but its customer-agent feature has separate subscription and credit requirements.</p><p>These models are not directly comparable without the same assumptions. Build a simple cost sheet for your monthly website traffic, expected conversations, sales team size, AI usage, CRM and calendar integrations, and support requirements. Then confirm the quote and billing terms on the vendor's official page.</p>
<h2>Budget and migration checklist</h2><ol><li>Record your current Drift contract end date and the official retirement deadline that applies to your account.</li><li>Ask Salesloft to confirm billing, support, data access, export process and any partner migration offer.</li><li>List each Drift feature you actually use: chat, playbooks, account targeting, meeting booking, Drift Email, reporting and custom API integrations.</li><li>Get a written quote for the replacement, including seats, usage, onboarding, support and contract length.</li><li>Test the highest-value visitor paths before switching the live website widget.</li><li>Export data and check record counts before access ends. Keep a separate backup with access limited to the migration team.</li><li>Remove the old widget and replace any Drift Email or API workflows before January 31, 2027, or earlier if your contract ends sooner.</li></ol>
<h2>Drift pricing FAQ</h2><h3>What is the current price of Drift?</h3><p>Salesloft does not show a current public Drift price on its Chat Agents page checked October 30, 2026. Existing customers should use their signed agreement and ask their account team about the contract end date.</p><h3>When does Drift billing or access end?</h3><p>The official sunset FAQ says data access ends on January 31, 2027 or at contract end, whichever comes first. For billing, contracts ending before January 31, 2027 are honored with no changes; contracts extending beyond that date are handled case by case.</p><h3>Can a new customer sign up for Drift?</h3><p>The current Salesloft Chat Agents page says it has transitioned from Drift to 1mind and does not show a public Drift purchase or pricing path.</p><h3>What should I budget for instead?</h3><p>Price the replacement based on seats, AI usage, website traffic, routing, CRM connections and migration work. The <a href="/drift/alternatives/">Drift alternatives guide</a> links to current official pricing pages for tools with public rates.</p>
