   'title'=>'How to Use Drift Before Retirement: Setup and Export',
   'seo_title'=>'How to Use Drift: Setup, Playbooks and Export',
   'description'=>'Follow documented Drift widget, playbook, reporting and export steps, then plan your migration before the January 31, 2027 retirement date for your team.',
   'url'=>'/drift/how-to-use/','date'=>'2026-10-30','updated'=>'2026-10-30','status'=>'published','author'=>'Deepak Parmar','breadcrumb_parent_name'=>'Drift','breadcrumb_parent_url'=>'/drift/',
   'faqs'=>[
    ['question'=>'Can I still use Drift before the retirement date?','answer'=>'Existing customers may continue under their contract until January 31, 2027 or their contract end date, whichever comes first, according to the official sunset FAQ checked October 30, 2026.'],
    ['question'=>'Where do I find the Drift install code?','answer'=>'The official Manage Chatbot Settings guide says to open Settings, choose Chatbot under App Settings, and use the Install tab to copy the relevant JavaScript, WordPress, Google Tag Manager or Drupal code.'],
    ['question'=>'How do I export Drift data?','answer'=>'The official sunset FAQ tells customers to contact their Account Manager or Support for export requests. Confirm which data types and formats are available and the deadline for your contract.'],
